    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Physical Survey:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Movers verify the video data, measure doorways, and inspect the condition of furniture and fixtures.</p>
  </div>
  <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.75); border: 1.5px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 14px; padding: 24px 20px; box-shadow: 0 10px 25px rgba(0,0,0,0.35); transition: transform 0.2s ease, border-color 0.2s ease;">
    <div style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; width: 42px; height: 42px; border-radius: 10px; background: #3b82f622; color: #3b82f6; font-weight: 800; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 14px;">03</div>
    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Inventory &amp; Fragility Log:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Every item is tagged with a unique code, noting its weight, material, and special handling needs.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<p>With the data in hand, the packing crew follows a systematic room‑by‑room strategy. Each room receives its own dedicated team, ensuring that items are grouped logically—electronics, kitchenware, bedroom linens—reducing cross‑room contamination and simplifying unboxing later.</p>

<ul>
<li><strong>Room Segmentation:</strong> Items are sorted by type and value; high‑value or fragile pieces receive custom cushioning.</li>
<li><strong>Labeling System:</strong> Boxes are color‑coded and labeled with room names and content descriptions.</li>
<li><strong>Protective Measures:</strong> Heavy furniture is disassembled where possible, and all components are secured with straps and blankets.</li>
</ul>

<p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">Transit is managed with a dedicated logistics plan.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The transport vehicle is pre‑loaded in reverse order of the destination layout, guaranteeing that the last box loaded is the first to be unloaded.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>GPS tracking and temperature control (if needed for electronics) are standard.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>Drivers follow a pre‑mapped route that avoids low bridges and heavy traffic, ensuring a smooth journey.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
<li><strong>Loading Sequence:</strong> Heavier, sturdier boxes at the bottom; fragile items on top.</li>
<li><strong>Route Optimization:</strong> Real‑time traffic updates guide the driver to the fastest, safest path.</li>
<li><strong>Safety Checks:</strong> Regular brake and tire inspections during stops.</li>
</ul>

<p>Upon arrival, the uncrating phase begins. The same room‑by‑room methodology is reversed: boxes are placed in their designated spots, labeled boxes are opened first, and all items are verified against the inventory list.</p>
<p>Movers handle the final assembly of furniture, ensuring that everything is set up exactly as it was before the move. The client’s satisfaction is confirmed with a walk‑through, and any discrepancies are addressed immediately.</p></div>
